Since most skilled nethack players seem to be of the opinion that the
score is relatively meaningless (since even a lame players like me can
run up arbitarily large scores by, e.g. pudding farming), it seems that
giving 5 points (to clan score, I guess) for each individual class is
not rewarding the things that matter. I suggest that the individual
class awards be expanded in some fashion, e.g.:

    5 points for most (best combo?) conducts for each class,
    4 points for lowest scored ascension for each class,
    3 points for fastest (game turns) ascension for each class,
    2 points for first acsension for each class, and
    1 point for highest scored ascension for each class.

I'd like to see discussion about the ranking and and other factors that
might be used instead. I guess it's too late to see these changes made
for this year, but I hope they will be considered for next year. I think
these changes would more accurately measure and reward nethack skill.

